cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use XInt-Bench, please cite the software entry below. Replace it with the paper
  once that is published -- see `preferred-citation`, which is filled in at submission.
title: "XInt-Bench: explanation-integrity attacks on network intrusion detection"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark of prediction-preserving attacks on the post-hoc feature attributions that
  ML-based NIDS attach to their alerts, with per-instance detector-relative interventional
  labels, a realizable-flow constraint over the extractor's own arithmetic, and a downstream
  autonomous-consumer decision task. Ships the attacks, the integrity signals, the conformal
  calibration, and a one-command reproduction of every number in the paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bibers
    given-names: Ismail Mohammed I
    affiliation: Purdue University
    # orcid: TODO add before the Zenodo release
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sm3a96/Same-Alert-Different-Reason-Attribution-Rewriting-Attacks-on-Intrusion-Detectors-Explained-to-Machin"
keywords:
  - explainable AI
  - intrusion detection
  - adversarial machine learning
  - attribution attacks
  - conformal prediction
  - agentic security operations
